    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "of6hrdq",
      "content": "1 litre = 1000 millilitres"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "te6au2m",
      "content": "1 tonne = 1000 kilograms"
    },
    {
      "id": "26qqe1q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "DENSITY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i3082ft",
      "content": "Density is defined as mass per unit volume. Formula:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tek7swo",
      "content": "Density = Mass / Volume Unit: kg/m³"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1tctt0t",
      "content": "If density is more, object is heavier. If density is less, object is lighter."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f894jbe",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "67jmtlw",
      "content": "Iron sinks in water because its density is greater than water."
    },
    {
      "id": "25urnwp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "DIMENSIONAL FORMULA"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w2nbxr7",
      "content": "Dimensional formula represents the relation of a physical quantity with mass (M), length"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hvf8mjf",
      "content": "(L) and time (T)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5lq6m91",
      "content": "Speed = M⁰L¹T⁻¹ Acceleration = M⁰L¹T⁻² Force = M¹L¹T⁻²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gxjltb6",
      "content": "Work = M¹L²T⁻² Power = M¹L²T⁻³"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "d4vc0db",
      "content": "Pressure = M¹L⁻¹T⁻²"
    },
    {
      "id": "jtfrzhg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "USES OF DIMENSIONAL FORMULA"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Light year, Astronomical Unit (AU), and Parsec are units of length/distance, not time (1 Parsec = 3.26 Light Years).",
        "Radian measures plane angles while Steradian measures solid angles.",
        "Density of pure water is maximum at 4°C (1000 kg/m³ or 1 g/cm³).",
        "Dimensional analysis cannot be used to determine dimensionless constants or trigonometric functions."
      ],
      "id": "ivk3opa"
    },
